  "notable_quotes": [
    "Varying synthesis temperature from 160 to 220 °C produced four crystalline Zn2(datrz)2CO3 phases from the same building units, with two topologies and varied pore geometries.",
    "Zn2(datrz)2CO3-180, -200, and -220 share the same topology, but ligand rotations create sub-angstrom pore-size gradients that tune molecular recognition behavior.",
    "Adjusting solvothermal synthesis temperature precisely modulates pore structures in Zn2(datrz)2CO3 while preserving framework composition and overall connectivity."
